  <data name="About_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>A tutor that teaches, not one that does your homework</value></data>
  <data name="About_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>MatGPT Tutor follows the Socratic method: it asks questions and gives hints so the student finds the answer by themselves. Choose the mode that fits what you need.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Mode_Guide" xml:space="preserve"><value>One question or hint at a time. The final answer only comes after real attempts.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Mode_Explain" xml:space="preserve"><value>A simple definition, an everyday example, a worked example and a question to check understanding.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Mode_Check" xml:space="preserve"><value>Says if the answer is right, points to the step with the mistake and gives a hint to fix it.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Mode_Practice" xml:space="preserve"><value>One exercise at a time, harder when you succeed, easier when you struggle.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Privacy_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Anonymous progress</value></data>
  <data name="About_Privacy_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>No account and no personal data: an anonymous cookie lets the tutor remember your level and conversation in each subject for 90 days. You can delete everything with one click.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Safety_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Designed for young learners</value></data>
  <data name="About_Safety_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Age-appropriate answers, kind refusal of off-limits topics, and if a student seems unwell, the tutor encourages them to talk to a trusted adult.</value></data>
  <data name="About_Tech_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>How it's built</value></data>
  <data name="About_Tech_Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>ASP.NET Core (.NET 10), Claude API with streaming, Tailwind CSS + Preline UI, Markdown and math (KaTeX) rendering. Offline demo mode without an API key.</value></data>
